<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <!--
      The window background is the frame between the system splash and the first
      Compose frame. It is @color/launch_bg, which is also
      windowSplashScreenBackground below and LaunchOverlay's ground at t=0, so
      all three are the same resource and cannot disagree.

      It used to be a hardcoded #0E1E25 (iOS's DARK gradient bottom stop) in both
      modes, matched to a brand splash screen that no existing install ever
      reached. What actually followed it was MaterialTheme.background, #F5F5F5.
      So the comment claiming this "stops the white flash" described the thing
      that CAUSED it: a full screen dark to light flash on every launch, measured
      on a device.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.rostam_reader_app" parent="Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/launch_bg</item>
    </style>

    <!--
      Android 12+ owns the first frame: a solid colour plus one icon, centred in
      the window, in a 288dp slot whose art must fit a 192dp circle. So the
      shared t=0 state is the MARK ALONE. The full lockup cannot survive that
      slot at a legible size, which is the one place Android cannot copy iOS, and
      the wordmark becomes what the overlay's light adds.

      @drawable/launch_mark is per brand and generated by
      tools/whitelabel/gen-launch.py, which insets each brand's own silhouette to
      fit the keyline circle. LaunchOverlay draws the SAME drawable at the same
      size in the same place: the hand-off is jump free because the two sides
      share a file, not a number.

      There is deliberately no windowSplashScreenIconBackgroundColor. It would
      shrink the slot from 288dp to 240dp and put the mark in a coloured
      container the splash ground does not have.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.App.Starting" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/launch_bg</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/launch_mark</item>
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/Theme.rostam_reader_app</item>
    </style>
</resources>
